---
description: Distill durable, verified lessons from this session into local Markdown memory
argument-hint: "[topic or focus]"
---
Review the current conversation and distill reusable knowledge into the private
Markdown memory vault under `~/.pi/memory/`.

Focus: ${ARGUMENTS:-durable user preferences, project decisions, non-obvious lessons, and reusable technical knowledge}

Load the `persistent-memory` skill and inspect the relevant indexes and existing
notes before proposing changes. Preserve only a small number of confirmed,
non-sensitive facts that are likely to help a future session. Choose the
narrowest appropriate scope, merge with existing notes, resolve duplicates or
contradictions, and update relevant index links. Before the first write,
acquire an exclusive advisory lock on `~/.pi/memory.lock`. While continuously
holding that lock, verify that the vault is its own Jujutsu repository, create
one new specifically described `[π]` revision, apply the distillation against
current file contents, and snapshot the finished changes with
`jj -R "$HOME/.pi/memory" status`. Complete the transaction in one lock-holding
tool invocation.

Do not save temporary task state or implementation status in curated memory
notes; approved feature-specific state belongs only in its workspace plan and
is not part of ordinary distillation. Do not save full transcripts, secrets,
speculation, or material already covered by project instructions or
documentation. If nothing deserves durable memory, say so and
leave the vault unchanged without creating a revision. Otherwise summarize the
facts saved and the note paths changed.
